      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Theorem4.4 derivation in Section4 and essential spinorial local supports2.2/2.3 and3.1/3.3 are supplied. M is closed connected and six-dimensional, equipped with the chosen almost complex J, b1(M)=0 and integral_M(c1c2-c3)!=0. The result concerns the component of J in the space of almost complex structures, equivalently the orthogonal component after choosing a metric; it gives nilpotency, finite cyclic fundamental group and the stated free zero-differential minimal model with generator multiplicities b4,b3,b2. The fibration4.1 and the generator elimination are explicit author constructions. Prior section-space rationalization, Thom mapping-space calculation and Crabb–Sutherland fundamental-group theorem are identified background. No nilpotency of M, integrability of J or all-component connectedness is claimed; intersection and four-dimensional variants are contextual only."
      },
